From: songze <songze.cai@gl-inet.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ovpn-dco: free current skb on invalid transport

The successful-encryption path walks a list of GSO segments and detaches each
segment before handing it to the configured transport. In the defensive
default branch, consume the current segment rather than the original list
head. Reusing the list-head pointer can release the same skb more than once
if an invalid transport is observed while processing a multi-segment packet.

Normal UDP and TCP transports are unchanged.

--- a/drivers/net/ovpn-dco/ovpn.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ovpn-dco/ovpn.c
@@ -364,7 +364,7 @@ void ovpn_encrypt_work(struct work_struc
 					break;
 				default:
 					/* no transport configured yet */
-					consume_skb(skb);
+					consume_skb(curr);
 					break;
 				}
 			}
